2026-10-29T22:24:23.1358640Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1368047Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1459475Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1469033Z [0m
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1469631Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1470076Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1470246Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1470747Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1471264Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1471478Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1471675Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1472030Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1472216Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1472832Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1473577Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1474121Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1474538Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1474734Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1474990Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1475443Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1475767Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1476229Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1476404Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1476499Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1476624Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1476943Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1477327Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1480503Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1480613Z I will:
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1480769Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1481007Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1481512Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1482053Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1482543Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1482876Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1483217Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1483553Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1483845Z    /root
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1494608Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1495203Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1511784Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1512461Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1512774Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1513084Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1513546Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1525940Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1526577Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1535971Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1536677Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1537039Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1537196Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1537336Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1537519Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1537820Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1538344Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1538597Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1538734Z If you would like to
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1539030Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1539211Z 
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1539435Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1539758Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-29T22:24:23.1539905Z 
